Short:        AHI driver for SB Audigy SE (CA0106)
Author:       Mirq
Uploader:     mirziom@gmail.com (Mirq)
Type:         driver/audio
Version:      4.3
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     driver/audio/ahiusr_4.18.lha, driver/other/openpci68k.lha
Distribution: Aminet

ca0106.audio is an AHI v4 sub-driver for PCI sound cards with the Creative
CA0106 chip, such as the Sound Blaster Audigy SE (SB0570), on classic
Amigas with a PCI bridge driven by openpci.library.

Features
--------
- Stereo playback at 48 and 96 kHz, 16-bit and HiFi (24-bit) modes
- Full-duplex 16-bit stereo recording from Line, Mic, Aux or CD
- Hardware monitor: the Aux input goes straight to the output, so Paula
  sound can be played through the card's speakers with no CPU load
- cactl: shell mixer control (input, gain, monitor, output volume)
- Test tools: caprobe, catone, ahitest, ahistream, capci

Audio modes: $00CA0001-$00CA0004 (16 bit stereo/stereo++,
HiFi 24 bit stereo/stereo++). The $00CA mode ID is provisional.

Requirements
------------
- 68020 or better (tuned for 68060), AmigaOS 3.x, AHI 4.x
- openpci.library: OpenPCI 2.1, or openpci.library 3.x/40.x by
  Thomas Richter (P96 3.5+ with GRANTDIRECTACCESS=Yes in the graphics
  card's monitor icon, for DMA memory)
- 48 KB of PCI DMA memory (on a Prometheus: the Prometheus.card DMA area
  in graphics card memory, DMASIZE tooltype)

Tested on an A4000/68060 with Prometheus FireStorm, Radeon 9200,
OpenPCI 2.1 and AHI 4.18. Reported working on an A1200/68060 with
Mediator PCI 1200 TX, openpci.library 40.16, AmigaOS 3.2.3 and
GRANTDIRECTACCESS=Yes.

Installation
------------
Unpack the archive, open a shell in the CA0106 drawer and run

  execute Install-CA0106

then pick a "CA0106:" mode in Prefs/AHI (48000 Hz recommended).
To hear Paula through the card, connect the Amiga audio output to the
card's Aux input and add to S:User-Startup:

  cactl INPUT=AUX MONITOR=0

Known limitations
-----------------
- 44.1 kHz is not offered: the CA0106 analog DAC path does not support it
- 5.1 surround and S/PDIF output are not implemented yet
- A guru when opening the AHI mode requester was reported once and has
  not been reproduced

Reporting problems
------------------
Quit all AHI programs, open a shell in the CA0106 drawer and run

  execute CA0106-Debug

and answer its questions about the tone (speakers on the green jack),
then send RAM:CA0106-Debug.txt together with a description of the
problem (Guru number, which program, cold boot or warm reset).

History
-------
4.3 (27.11.2026)
- DMA memory is checked when AHI opens the card: every page must be
  where the card will look for it on the PCI bus, and data written by
  the CPU must read back after a cache flush. If not, AllocAudio fails
  with an error instead of playing silence
- A1200 Mediator with openpci.library 40.x reported working (P96 needs
  GRANTDIRECTACCESS=Yes)
- caprobe 0.3: bridge type, openpci address map, and where the DMA
  memory is (non-cacheable or not, bus address, Fast/Chip RAM)
- catone 0.3: VERIFY reports PASS/FAIL; GPIO=hex tries other analog
  output routings
- CA0106-Debug: lspci, PCI-Configuration, DMAMemTest, a digital loopback
  check, and listening tests (asks whether you heard a tone)
4.2 (25.11.2026)
- If the codecs do not answer during chip setup, AllocAudio now fails
  cleanly instead of running a silent card, and the next open runs the
  full setup again
- An I2C write that never completes is no longer reported as success
- New CA0106-Debug script that collects a diagnostic log
4.1 (18.11.2026)
- First release

Source code and issue tracker: https://github.com/mirq/ca0106-ahi

